      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Electricity"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Electric current is the rate of flow of electric charge through a conductor per unit of time.",
        "Voltage (potential difference) provides the electrical pressure required for current to flow.",
        "Ohm's Law states that electric current is directly proportional to voltage and inversely proportional to resistance.",
        "Magnetic poles always exist in pairs; magnetic monopoles do not exist.",
        "Electromagnets are temporary magnets whose strength depends on current magnitude and the number of coil turns."
      ],
      "id": "1rhjpbs"
