    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "An ammeter is always connected in series due to its very low resistance, whereas a voltmeter is connected in parallel due to its high resistance.",
        "Soft iron is preferred for making electromagnet cores because of its high permeability and low retentivity.",
        "Fuse wires are made of alloys with low melting points and high resistivity, always connected in series with the live wire."
